title Stricter cannot be contained
prompt Keaton, mid-lap: New Gauge and New Gauge Radiant should both have the best of the elder, and we may want to archive the elders if they are contained within Gauge now -- whatever you recommend.
rota none -- a recommendation asked mid-lap; the Water row was read at 20260908.141457, which is the lap this answer grew out of.
think The question is whether Gauge contains Radiant and Twilight, and containment is a fact about two files rather than a matter of taste, so it can be measured rather than argued.
obs GAUGE CANNOT CONTAIN RADIANT, AND THE LATTICE SEATED THIS AFTERNOON IS THE PROOF. Gauge RELAXES the negation floor to 20 percent so a measured page may say what refused; Radiant holds it at ZERO. A register stricter on an axis cannot be contained by the one that loosens it. Archiving Radiant would delete the strictest row of a table written the same day.
obs AND TWILIGHT CARRIES AN AXIS GAUGE NEVER NAMES AT ALL. Poetry appears nowhere in Gauge's own headings; it is Twilight's whole contribution. Two axes need both parents.
obs THE CITATION READING AGREES AND IS THE CHEAPER ARGUMENT. Living files citing each guide: Gauge 923, Radiant 129, Twilight 76, Bhakta 4. Radiant and Twilight are not vestigial pages kept from sentiment -- 205 living files reach for them by name, and every reference is a promise already made.
obs WHAT GAUGE GENUINELY INHERITS IS WARMTH AND CLARITY, WHICH ITS OWN HEADER ALREADY SAYS. Its Inherits line names Radiant for exactly that. What it does not inherit is the floor or the poetry, and those are precisely what the elder pages carry. A guide is archived when nothing needs it.
obs SO THE RECOMMENDATION IS KEEP, AND THE ANSWER IS RECORDED IN GAUGE ITSELF. A question asked once and answered in a session log gets asked again in a month; answered beside the Inherits line it claimed to supersede, it stays answered.
loom guides gauge_lines=689 radiant=329 twilight=98 bhakta=? citations_gauge=923 radiant=129 twilight=76 bhakta=4
loom containment gauge_floor=20pct radiant_floor=0pct poetry_in_gauge=absent verdict=not_contained
file context/GAUGE_STYLE.md the containment question asked and answered beside the Inherits line
scope one recommendation answered by measuring containment rather than by preference
status GREEN -- tracked links ok, ascii ok, Gauge grading 92 at the Door setting after the addition
recommend keep-going -- Bhakta at four citations is the one genuinely new register and the one worth spending reach on; the elders have 205 between them and need nothing.
